  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Location and Function
    
    A Nightshelf forge-temple carved into The Berg's eastern reaches, three hundred fathoms down where volcanic veins warm the surrounding stone. The Thewsed Slew~ sits at the junction of deep-water trade routes, its fire-cores providing geothermal heat critical to the colony's infrastructure. Locals call it *the Slew* — never "the temple," never "the forge." The distinction matters to them.
    
    ## History of Violence
    
    The main chamber's eastern wall bears orca-claw gouges from the Orca Incursion, deep enough to fit a flipper. The Nightshelf patched them with salvage-stone that does not match the original. It was during or shortly after the Incursion that the Grend Blood-Arts — a unified orca combat doctrine binding blood-sense, pressure-strike, and deep-communion — were recovered here from texts originating in The Whispered Shrift~, a contested deep-tunnel site. The recovery was documented in The Nighted~ Lantern, an artifact whose current disposition I have not confirmed.
    
    The second desecration came later, during the Three-Day Dark, when the Wake-Singers — orca shamans devoted to waking their dead god through accumulated sacrifice — breached the Slew and tore open cleansed ground at the memorial stones. Three shamans died in the working. The dark-stains left on the lower altars have resisted all subsequent fire-scrubbing. ☽'Otrolal the Watchful performed the cleansing that followed.
    
    A carved mark on the northern support-beam records three names and a date. No source identifies whose flipper held the blade.
    
    ## The Lower Levels
    
    The ice beneath the Slew holds pressure-readable impressions of what was inflicted here — orca kill-songs and penguin screams pressed into stone. The Shelf Crushing Offense's sorcery during the Wake-Singer breach resonated through the temple's structure; the ice caught it. The pressure-song produced during that working was audible as far as the Still Pools.
    
    Deeper still, where Berg-ice meets the first volcanic stone, lies what the elders call *memory-ice*: material old enough to hold impressions permanently. It was here that the orca weapon Grungruk's Claw — a trident carrying the dying rage of its former wielder, Zund Gnasharkin — was entombed by Grul Grulrend, an orca who chose burial over further bloodshed. The weapon remains.
    
    Side-channels from the Wake-Singer era riddle the surrounding rock, corrupted beyond reading even by fire-sutured senses. Sightings of unidentified presences — neither orca-shape nor penguin — in the eastern reaches have prompted guild-masters to restrict passage to lit corridors east of the forge-vents.
    
    ## Current Status
    
    The Slew remains operational. Its fire-cores still burn, still warm the trade routes, still keep the colony's heart beating. Custody is maintained by those old enough to remember what happened here and cautious enough not to forget it. The ice, of course, has no choice in the matter.
